# CombatCall landing + SEO build env.
#
# NOTE: SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_ANON_KEY and their PUBLIC_ twins are the SAME
# Supabase project URL + anon key — copy the same two values into both pairs.
# The split exists only because of WHERE each is read:
#   - non-PUBLIC_  → read by the build (data.ts, server-side at build time)
#   - PUBLIC_      → inlined into the client bundle (EmailGate.astro) by Vite
# They are not four different credentials.
#
# Build-time (server) — data.ts fetches the upcoming card at build time:
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Client (shipped in the bundle; public-by-design like the app's anon key):
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# PostHog (optional — no key = analytics no-op). phc_ key is public-by-design.
PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# Meta (Facebook) Pixel (optional — no ID = pixel no-op). Public-by-design.
# Drives ad-conversion tracking on the /ufc/ SEO pages (PageView + Lead).
#
# NOTE: the hand-written homepage public/index.html is served VERBATIM (Astro
# does not process it), so PUBLIC_* injection does NOT reach it. Its pixel ID is
# read at runtime from window.__META_PIXEL_ID__ (set in a small inline config
# block in that file). When the pixel exists, set this env var AND the homepage
# config value to the SAME id. See public/index.html + this repo's README.
PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=
